{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 16,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then Job answered and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have heard many such things: miserable comforters ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ye all.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shall vain words have an end? or what emboldeneth thee that thou answerest?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I also could speak as ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "do",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": if your soul were in my soul's stead, I could heap up words against you, and shake my head at you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I would strengthen you with my mouth and the moving of my lips should assuage ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "your grief",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though I speak, my grief is not assuaged: and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "though",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I forbear, what am I eased?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But now he hath made me weary: thou hast made desolate all my company.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou hast filled me with wrinkles, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is a witness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "against me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": and my leanness rising up in me beareth witness to my face.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He teareth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in his wrath, who hateth me: he gnasheth upon me with his teeth; my enemy sharpeneth his eyes upon me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have gaped upon me with their mouth; they have smitten me upon the cheek reproachfully; they have gathered themselves against me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God hath delivered me to the ungodly, and turned me over into the hands of the wicked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I was at ease, but he hath broken me asunder: he hath also taken ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "me",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by my neck, and shaken me to pieces, and set me up for his mark.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His archers encompass me; he cleaveth my reins asunder, and doth not spare; he poureth out my gall upon the ground.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He breaketh me with breach upon breach, he runneth upon me like a giant.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have sewed sackcloth upon my skin, and defiled my horn in the dust.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My face is foul with weeping, and on my eyelids ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the shades of death;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Not for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "any",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " injustice in my hands: also my prayer ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " pure.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O earth, cover not thou my blood, and let my cry have no place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also now, behold, my witness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in heaven, and my record ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on high.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My friends scorn me: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my eye poureth out ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "tears",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O that one might plead for a man with God, as a man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "pleadeth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for his neighbor!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.16.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.16.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When a few years are come, then I shall go the way ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "whence",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I shall not return.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
